{
  "reports": [
    {
      "title": "Feeder 47 Restoration Lockout Due to Relay Setting Mismatch at Synthetic Substation 5",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "At 09:22, a synthetic tree branch contacted feeder 47's primary conductor, causing relay 52-47 to open.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The SCADA operator at Synthetic Control initiated remote closing of feeder breaker 52-47 at 09:31 after repairs were reported complete.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [0]
        },
        {
          "text": "When breaker 52-47 closed, transformer bank TB-5 magnetizing inrush reached 1.9 kiloamperes.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [1]
        },
        {
          "text": "Cold load pickup of 8.6 megawatts drew 640 amperes for the first 1.5 minutes after the closure.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [0, 1]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ground relay 51G-47's pickup was set to 150 amperes, while the magnetizing inrush produced 1.9 kiloamperes.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Relay 27-47's undervoltage block was configured to release after 1 second, matching the dead-line check time exactly.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Root cause was mismatched setting between relay 51G-47 and relay 27-47, because inrush could not be distinguished.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": [4, 5]
        },
        {
          "text": "The lockout was not caused by feeder overload; only the ground relay's low threshold prevented restoration.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "After the 1.9 kiloampere inrush exceeded pickup, relay 51G-47 issued a trip command in 45 milliseconds.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [2, 4]
        },
        {
          "text": "The distribution management system locked out feeder 47, stopping the restoration sequence and blocking remote closure.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "Later, the crew manually closed feeder 47's bypass switch, providing backfeed from Synthetic Feeder 12, but only for 20 minutes.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "Because the bypass backfeed exceeded Feeder 12's emergency rating, operators opened the tie switch immediately.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [3, 10]
        },
        {
          "text": "The failed restoration left 1,400 Synthetic customers without power for three hours, undercounted as a 12 megawatt-hour outage.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "No physical equipment was damaged because the 200 millisecond backup interrupter removed the false fault before thermal stress.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The misoperation degraded the region's quarterly availability statistic by 0.04 percent at Synthetic Substation 5.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "Synthetic Feeder 12 returned to normal after the tie switch opened, but no additional load was served.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [11]
        },
        {
          "text": "Engineers uploaded corrected settings to relay 51G-47, raising pickup to 500 amperes with harmonic restraint enabled.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [4]
        },
        {
          "text": "Only if a zero-voltage check remains true for 20 seconds will breaker 52-47 reclose after a lockout.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [5]
        },
        {
          "text": "An automated playback test using the recorded 1.9 kiloampere inrush confirmed that the new settings reject the transient.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [2, 16]
        },
        {
          "text": "The corrective action notice mandated quarterly audits of all feeder protection setting groups in Synthetic Region 9.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [6]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Feeder 9 Restoration Trip Caused by Capacitor Inrush Setting Miscoordination",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "At 13:05, lightning struck Synthetic North Feeder 9, causing a phase-to-phase fault and tripping the feeder breaker.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "After a successful 80 second dead-line test, operators issued an automatic restoration sequence at 14:22.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [0]
        },
        {
          "text": "Closing breaker 52-9 energized the 12.5 MVA transformer block, driving magnetizing inrush to 1.1 kiloamperes.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [1]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 14:23, the automatic capacitor bank controller switched on the 40 Mvar capacitor bank, producing 780 amperes of inrush.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [2]
        },
        {
          "text": "The neutral overcurrent relay 51N-9 had a pickup of 240 amperes, which is less than the capacitor inrush.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The restoration logic allowed breaker 52-9 to close while bus residual voltage remained at 35 percent.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The capacitor sectionalizer's 500 millisecond delay did not coordinate with recloser R-9's 200 millisecond fast curve.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The lockout was not caused by transformer inrush because harmonic restraint supervised the phase element correctly.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": [2]
        },
        {
          "text": "The 780 ampere capacitor inrush created a net neutral current of 620 amperes through relay 51N-9.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [3]
        },
        {
          "text": "Because 620 amperes exceeded the 240 ampere pickup, recloser R-9 locked out after only two fast operations.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [4, 8]
        },
        {
          "text": "The sectionalizer waited 500 milliseconds for the fast curve, but recloser R-9 had already locked out after two operations.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [6, 9]
        },
        {
          "text": "A tie breaker to Synthetic Feeder 11 closed for restoration, but residual voltage mismatch caused it to trip in 120 milliseconds.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [5, 9]
        },
        {
          "text": "Synthetic North Feeder 9's 2,050 customers remained without power for 2.7 hours due to the failed restoration.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9, 11]
        },
        {
          "text": "No capacitor damage occurred because the bank fuse rated at 1,200 amperes did not melt under the 780 ampere inrush.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [3, 9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The fast tripping produced voltage flicker of 6.2 percent on Synthetic Bus 4 for about 45 seconds.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "No outage occurred on Synthetic Feeder 11 because the tie breaker isolated the mismatch in 120 milliseconds.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [11]
        },
        {
          "text": "Maintenance staff raised relay 51N-9's pickup to 800 amperes and enabled capacitor switching restraint logic.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [4]
        },
        {
          "text": "Only if bus residual voltage decays to zero for 30 seconds will breaker 52-9 be permitted to close.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [5]
        },
        {
          "text": "An updated playback test uses the recorded 780 ampere inrush to verify that relay 51N-9 will restrain every six months.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [3, 16]
        },
        {
          "text": "A single change request aligned recloser R-9, sectionalizer, and capacitor controller settings after the incident.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [6]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
